Lab 9: Resilient Deep Learning Architectures with Failover Strategies
Objective
Simulate a resilient deep learning deployment by running model replicas, implementing health checks, and automatically rerouting traffic if a model instance fails — all locally without needing the cloud.

Prerequisites
Start your Al Nafi-provided Ubuntu machine

Ensure the following are installed:

Python 3.8+

Flask (pip install flask)

requests Python package (pip install requests)

Steps
Step 1: Launch Replica Model Instances
Create two model replicas:
Replica 1 (port 5001)
mkdir -p ~/dl-failover-lab/replica1
cd ~/dl-failover-lab/replica1
cat > app.py <<EOF
from flask import Flask, jsonify
app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route('/predict', methods=['GET'])
def predict():
    return jsonify({"model": "replica1", "prediction": "class-A"})

@app.route('/health', methods=['GET'])
def health():
    return jsonify({"status": "healthy"})

if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(port=5001)
EOF
Replica 2 (port 5002)
mkdir -p ~/dl-failover-lab/replica2
cd ~/dl-failover-lab/replica2
cat > app.py <<EOF
from flask import Flask, jsonify
app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route('/predict', methods=['GET'])
